{"hash": "4fcc0c7ffc41e291", "text": "And every landlord keeps a logbook. First, training. Claude's Free, Pro and Max plans, Claude Code included, have a setting: Help improve our AI models. On, data can be kept up to five years; off, deleted chats are purged within thirty days. Pro is a consumer plan; Team, Enterprise and the A P I are commercial. Switching it off doesn't reach training already started. Second, memory is a separate store. Delete a chat; its memories stay until you delete them too. Third, keep work and home in separate accounts; shared logins aren't supported. Others differ: Google has humans review some Gemini chats, and keeps reviewed ones up to three years, even after you delete your activity. Ask any tool four questions. Is there a training setting? Do people review chats? How long is data kept with it off? What does deleting reach? The picture's last break: leaving a room doesn't take every copy with you.", "alignment": {"characters": ["A", "n", "d", " ", "e", "v", "e", "r", "y", " ", "l", "a", "n", "d", "l", "o", "r", "d", " ", "k", "e", "e", "p", "s", " ", "a", " ", "l", "o", "g", "b", "o", "o", "k", ".", " ", "F", "i", "r", "s", "t", ",", " ", "t", "r", "a", "i", "n", "i", "n", "g", ".", " ", "C", "l", "a", "u", "d", "e", "'", "s", " ", "F", "r", "e", "e", ",", " ", "P", "r", "o", " ", "a", "n", "d", " ", "M", "a", "x", " ", "p", "l", "a", "n", "s", ",", " ", "C", "l", "a", "u", "d", "e", " ", "C", "o", "d", "e", " ", "i", "n", "c", "l", "u", "d", "e", "d", ",", " ", "h", "a", "v", "e", " ", "a", " ", "s", "e", "t", "t", "i", "n", "g", ":", " ", "H", "e", "l", "p", " ", "i", "m", "p", "r", "o", "v", "e", " ", "o", "u", "r", " ", "A", "I", " ", "m", "o", "d", "e", "l", "s", ".", " ", "O", "n", ",", " ", "d", "a", "t", "a", " ", "c", "a", "n", " ", "b", "e", " ", "k", "e", "p", "t", " ", "u", "p", " ", "t", "o", " ", "f", "i", "v", "e", " ", "y", "e", "a", "r", "s", ";", " ", "o", "f", "f", ",", " ", "d", "e", "l", "e", "t", "e", "d", " ", "c"